# Agent sensor pipeline (mandatory)

This is the **only** navigation flow. Do not invent a fourth sensor. Do not keep two hot.

```
mashed-up code / where-does-X-live / FastAPI↔PHP
        │ Step 1
   GRAPHIFY CLI  (Graphify-Labs/graphify)
        │ Steps 2–3
   CODEGRAPH MCP (@colbymchenry/codegraph)
        │ Steps 4–6
   RIPWIRE CLI   (redhat-et/ripwire)
```

Never install, query, or keep Graphify, CodeGraph, and Ripwire in the same session.

## Pins (do not swap)

| Step | Role in the diagram | PCD pin | Interface |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Graphify-Labs/graphify | `graphify` 0.9.x · `graphify-out/` · `ARCHITECTURE.md` | **CLI only.** Do not add `graphify-mcp` to `.cursor/mcp.json`. |
| 2–3 | CodeGraph via MCP | `@colbymchenry/codegraph` in `.cursor/mcp.json` · index `.codegraph/` | **MCP** (`codegraph_explore`). Do **not** install `codegraph-ai/CodeGraph` (42-tool MCP blows the token SLO). |
| 4–6 | redhat-et/ripwire | `ripwire` 0.6.x at `~/.local/bin` · `--cache=.ripwire` | **CLI only.** Do not add `ripwire --mcp` to `.cursor/mcp.json`. |

If a pin is missing: Graphify `uv tool install graphifyy`. Ripwire: `RIPWIRE_REPO=redhat-et/ripwire RIPWIRE_INSTALL_YES=1 RIPWIRE_NO_ACTIVATE=1 bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/redhat-et/ripwire/main/scripts/install.sh)"`. CodeGraph: `npx -y @colbymchenry/codegraph init` (MCP already in `.cursor/mcp.json`).

## Moment A — Graphify (architecture only)

Use when the question is global: mashed-up dependencies, “where does X live”, god nodes, FastAPI ↔ Fleetbase PHP, path between two systems.

- First run: `graphify extract . --code-only` then `graphify cluster-only . --no-label --no-viz`
- Query: `graphify query "…"`, `graphify path A B`, `graphify explain X`, `graphify god-nodes`
- Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` + `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` before grepping
- After a **folder-graph** change: `graphify update .`. Not after every line edit.

This rule **overrides** `.cursor/rules/graphify.mdc` for daily coding.

## Moment B — CodeGraph (schemas + Maps/OSRM/Valhalla/Vroom)

Activate **before** extracting Pydantic/ORM or moving routing logic.

- MCP: `codegraph_explore` (primary). Optional follow-ups: `codegraph_search`, `codegraph_callers`, `codegraph_impact`
- If MCP is not in this session: `npx -y @colbymchenry/codegraph explore "<query>" --path .`
- VROOM stays behind the Fleetbase orchestrator — do not invent a PorterChain VROOM client

## Moment C — Ripwire (thin routers, Stripe/Clerk adapters, client views)

CLI first. Skip Ripwire MCP.

```
ripwire . --cache=.ripwire --for="<the change in words>"
ripwire . --cache=.ripwire --callers=SYM
ripwire . --cache=.ripwire --expand=SYM
ripwire . --cache=.ripwire --impact=SYM
```

Do not start Ripwire during Graphify mapping or CodeGraph indexing.

## Forbidden

- Grep/Read dump of a portal or engine “to be safe”
- Installing `codegraph-ai/CodeGraph` or a second CodeGraph
- Wiring Graphify or Ripwire into `.cursor/mcp.json` (CodeGraph is the only MCP sensor)
- Running all three sensors in one session
